\ cv8t.4 - cv8.4 under the two-bit tag (Iteration 67, FORMAT-TAG2.md): 64
\ one-byte opcodes and an escape, calls of 2, 3, 4 bytes (14, 22, 30 bits:
\ a 1 GB code space), links of 1-4 bytes. A copy - the original is frozen by
\ the designs recorded with it. The opcode constants keep their logical
\ values here; layout.py --tag2 rewrites each to this design's code.
\ cv8.4 - make the Forth compiler emit CV8 instead of cells.
\
\ CV8: Compressed-pointer, Variable-length, 8-bit units.
\
\ Phase 3. Until now every CV8 image has been TRANSLATED from a cell
\ image by tools/layout.py, so a CV8 system could run but could not
\ compile a new definition.
\ This file replaces the code-emitting words with CV8 emitters.
\
\ HOW IT IS USED. Every word here has a distinct name (`;8`, `IF8`, ...)
\ because redefining `;` in the CELL image would break the cell
\ compiler on the very next definition. Load this, dump, and translate
\ with --cv8-compiler, which swaps each `X8` body into `X`. The overlay's own bodies are compiled by the cell
\ compiler and translated like any other word; what changes is that the
\ RESULTING image's compiler emits bytes. The cell image keeps its own
\ compiler untouched, so relf/relf32 are unaffected.
\
\ WHAT IS NOT TOUCHED. `,` and `C,` still append data - VARIABLE, ALLOT
\ and the dictionary header all rely on them. Only the words that
\ append CODE are redefined.
\
\ See CV8-REFERENCE.md for the encoding this emits.

\ ---- opcode numbers (CV8-REFERENCE.md 3.2) --------------------------
\ The primitive band is kernel.4's PRIMITIVE order, so these are fixed
\ small integers rather than the cell image's code-field addresses.
  1 CONSTANT EXIT-OP
  2 CONSTANT LIT16-OP
  3 CONSTANT BRANCH-OP
  4 CONSTANT 0BRANCH-OP
 68 CONSTANT LIT32-OP
 69 CONSTANT DOVAR-OP
 70 CONSTANT DODOES-OP
 71 CONSTANT LIT8-OP
124 CONSTANT LIT64-OP           \ 0x7C
 63 CONSTANT ESC-OP             \ tag 2: the escape, always 0x3F
  0 CONSTANT BRANCH8-OP         \ tag 2: the short branches, if this design
  0 CONSTANT ?BRANCH8-OP        \ has them (layout.py writes their codes)

\ ---- raw emission ---------------------------------------------------
: OP, ( n --- )
\ Append one opcode byte.
  C, ;

: W, ( n --- )
\ Append a 16-bit little-endian operand.
  DUP 255 AND C, 8 RSHIFT 255 AND C, ;

: 32, ( n --- )
\ Append a 32-bit little-endian operand.
  DUP W, 16 RSHIFT W, ;

VARIABLE CV8-SHIFT-V ( --- a-addr )
\ The call/slot scale. 3 on a 64-bit cell, 2 on a 32-bit cell - or 0 in
\ the byte-granular-header layout, where cv8b.4 sets it. A VARIABLE and
\ not a constant so a second overlay can change it after this one is
\ loaded; everything below reads it through CV8-SHIFT.
: CV8-SHIFT-DEFAULT ( --- n ) 1 CELLS 8 = IF 3 ELSE 2 THEN ;
CV8-SHIFT-DEFAULT CV8-SHIFT-V !
: CV8-SHIFT ( --- n ) CV8-SHIFT-V @ ;

VARIABLE CV8-DOES-FAR? ( --- a-addr )
VARIABLE CV8-DOES-RESERVE ( --- a-addr )
\ How DOES> writes its call, and how much room CREATE leaves for it.
\ Two bytes by default; cv8b.4 sets three, because at a call scale of 0
\ the near form cannot reach past 16 KB.
-1 CV8-DOES-FAR? ! 4 CV8-DOES-RESERVE !   \ tag 2: the 4-byte call, always

VARIABLE LAST-OP ( --- a-addr )
\ Address of the primitive opcode just emitted, or 0 if the last thing
\ emitted cannot be folded.

\ ---- literals -------------------------------------------------------
: LIT, ( n --- )
\ Append a literal in the narrowest form that holds it. U< does the
\ range tests, so a negative value falls through to the wide forms.
  0 LAST-OP !
  DUP 256 U<   IF LIT8-OP  OP, C, EXIT THEN
  DUP 65536 U< IF LIT16-OP OP, W, EXIT THEN
  1 CELLS 4 = IF LIT32-OP OP, 32, EXIT THEN
  \ 64-bit cell: does it fit a SIGNED 32-bit field? n + 2^31 < 2^32.
  DUP 2147483648 + 4294967296 U< IF LIT32-OP OP, 32, EXIT THEN
  \ Wider than 32 bits needs a full cell. Before LIT64 existed such a
  \ value was silently truncated (CV8-REFERENCE.md 10).
  LIT64-OP OP, DUP 32, 32 RSHIFT 32, ;

: LITERAL8 ( n --- )
\ Add a literal to the current definition.
  LIT, ; IMMEDIATE

\ ---- folding prim;EXIT at runtime ------------------------------------
\ The translator folds a primitive followed by EXIT into one opcode
\ (CV8-REFERENCE.md 6.4), worth ~20%. Without this, code compiled at
\ RUN time misses that; with it, newly compiled code matches translated
\ code. Two things make it safe:
\   * the fold applies only to the LAST op of a definition, at `;`, so
\     nothing can branch past it into the EXIT;
\   * LAST-OP is cleared by anything that is not a plain primitive emit,
\     including every branch resolution - a THEN that resolves to HERE
\     would otherwise be left pointing at an EXIT that is no longer
\     there.

: >OP ( xt --- n )
\ The CV8 opcode of a PRIMITIVE, computed in the CELL image where this
\ file is compiled: a cell-image primitive token is 1 + n * CELL, and n
\ is exactly the CV8 opcode (both are the position in kernel.4).
  @ 1- 1 CELLS / ;

CREATE FOLD-OPS ( --- a-addr )
\ The foldable primitives as OPCODE BYTES, in the SAME ORDER as the
\ translator's --fold-set and the engine's generated table. Bytes, not
\ xts: an xt is an absolute address of the cell session and would not
\ survive translation - the first version of this stored xts and read
\ back garbage.
  ' + >OP C,  ' = >OP C,  ' ! >OP C,  ' @ >OP C,
  ' LSHIFT >OP C,  ' RSHIFT >OP C,  ' C@ >OP C,  ' C! >OP C,
  ' AND >OP C,  ' OR >OP C,  ' XOR >OP C,  ' LIT >OP C,
  ' < >OP C,  ' U< >OP C,  ' OVER >OP C,  ' DROP >OP C,
  ' DUP >OP C,  ' SWAP >OP C,  ' ROT >OP C,  ' >R >OP C,
  ' R> >OP C,  ' R@ >OP C,  ' NEGATE >OP C,
ALIGN
23 CONSTANT #FOLD-OPS
73 CONSTANT FOLD-BASE

: FOLD-OP ( op --- op2 -1 | op 0 )
\ The folded opcode for primitive opcode op, if it has one.
  #FOLD-OPS 0 DO
    DUP FOLD-OPS I + C@ = IF
      DROP I FOLD-BASE + -1 UNLOOP EXIT
    THEN
  LOOP 0 ;

\ ---- calls ----------------------------------------------------------
: CALL, ( a-addr --- )
\ Append a call to the body at a-addr: its byte offset from the image base
\ in the shortest form that reaches - 01 + 14 bits, 10 + 22, 11 + 30: k
\ more bytes after the first, the first holding k and the top bits. The
\ engine holds at most 1 GB (vm-lab.c, TAG2), so every offset fits.
  0 LAST-OP !
  START @ -  DUP 16384 < IF 1 ELSE DUP 4194304 < IF 2 ELSE 3 THEN THEN   ( v k )
  2DUP 3 LSHIFT RSHIFT OVER 6 LSHIFT OR C,
  BEGIN DUP WHILE 1- 2DUP 3 LSHIFT RSHIFT 255 AND C, REPEAT 2DROP ;

: COMPILE,8 ( xt --- )
\ Add the execution semantics of xt to the current definition: a
\ primitive becomes its opcode byte, anything else a call.
  DUP >NAME C@ 32 AND IF
    \ A primitive's CV8 body is one opcode byte - C@, not @: the cell
    \ compiler read a whole cell here because a token WAS a cell.
    \ An escaped primitive's body is [ESC][selector]; inline both bytes
    \ and do not offer it for folding.
    DUP C@ ESC-OP = IF
      DUP C@ OP, 1+ C@ OP, 0 LAST-OP !
    ELSE
      C@ HERE LAST-OP ! OP,
    THEN
  ELSE
    CALL,
  THEN ;

: ;8 ( --- )
\ Finish the current definition.
  LAST-OP @ DUP IF
    DUP C@ FOLD-OP IF SWAP C! ELSE 2DROP EXIT-OP OP, THEN
  ELSE DROP EXIT-OP OP, THEN
  0 LAST-OP ! 0 STATE ! ?CSP REVEAL ; IMMEDIATE

\ ---- control flow ---------------------------------------------------
\ A branch operand is a signed 16-bit BYTE offset measured from the
\ operand itself (CV8-REFERENCE.md 3.3) - not from past it, and not in
\ cells. >MARK leaves the operand's address for >RESOLVE to patch.

: >MARK ( --- a-addr )
\ Emit a placeholder branch operand and leave its address.
  0 LAST-OP ! HERE 0 W, ;

: !W ( n a-addr --- )
\ Store a 16-bit little-endian value.
  2DUP C! 1+ SWAP 8 RSHIFT 255 AND SWAP C! ;

: >RESOLVE ( a-addr --- )
\ Patch the operand at a-addr so its branch lands on HERE. Clears
\ LAST-OP: something now branches HERE, so the op before it must not
\ be folded away.
  0 LAST-OP ! DUP HERE SWAP - SWAP !W ;

: <RESOLVE ( a-addr --- )
\ Emit a branch operand jumping back to a-addr.
  0 LAST-OP ! HERE - W, ;

: BEGIN8 ( --- a-addr )
  HERE ; IMMEDIATE

: <BRANCH, ( a-addr op8 op16 --- )
\ A branch back to a-addr: the one-byte offset if this design has the short
\ form and it reaches, else the 16-bit one (FORMAT-TAG2.md: a backward
\ branch's distance is known, so its length can follow it). Both offsets
\ count from the operand, which follows the opcode's one byte.
  >R DUP IF
    OVER HERE 1+ - DUP -128 < 0= IF ROT DROP SWAP OP, C, R> DROP 0 LAST-OP ! EXIT THEN
    DROP
  THEN DROP R> OP, <RESOLVE ;

: UNTIL8 ( a-addr --- )
  ?BRANCH8-OP 0BRANCH-OP <BRANCH, ; IMMEDIATE

: AGAIN8 ( a-addr --- )
  BRANCH8-OP BRANCH-OP <BRANCH, ; IMMEDIATE

: IF8 ( --- a-addr )
  0BRANCH-OP OP, >MARK ; IMMEDIATE

: THEN8 ( a-addr --- )
  >RESOLVE ; IMMEDIATE

: ELSE8 ( a-addr1 --- a-addr2 )
  BRANCH-OP OP, >MARK SWAP >RESOLVE ; IMMEDIATE

: WHILE8 ( a-addr1 --- a-addr2 a-addr1 )
  POSTPONE IF8 SWAP ; IMMEDIATE

: REPEAT8 ( a-addr1 a-addr2 --- )
  \ ( a-addr1 a-addr2 --- ) with the BEGIN address on top, as WHILE8
  \ left it: <RESOLVE takes that one, >RESOLVE patches WHILE's mark.
  BRANCH8-OP BRANCH-OP <BRANCH, >RESOLVE ; IMMEDIATE

\ ---- defining words -------------------------------------------------
: CREATE8 ( "ccc" --- )
\ A data body is [DOVAR][pad to a cell][parameter field], so the
\ parameter field stays cell-aligned and the pad is never executed.
  \ Two bytes reserved after DOVAR so that DOES> can overwrite the front
  \ with [DODOES][2-byte call] without moving the parameter field. The
  \ engine computes the PFA as align(body+3) on both paths.
  HEADER REVEAL DOVAR-OP OP, CV8-DOES-RESERVE @ ALLOT ALIGN ;

: VARIABLE8 ( "ccc" --- )
  CREATE8 0 , ;

: CONSTANT8 ( x "ccc" --- )
  HEADER REVEAL LIT, EXIT-OP OP, ;

: RECURSE8 ( --- )
  LAST @ NAME> CALL, ; IMMEDIATE

\ ---- DO ... LOOP ----------------------------------------------------
\ (LOOP) and (+LOOP) read an inline CELL operand, and it must stay
\ cell-aligned - the one place CV8 keeps cell granularity
\ (CV8-REFERENCE.md 3.3). The translator pads BEFORE the call so the
\ operand lands aligned just after it; the runtime compiler does the
\ same. The pad is NOOPs, which do execute, once per loop.
: OPERAND-ALIGN ( --- )
\ Emit NOOPs until a 2-byte call would leave HERE cell-aligned.
  BEGIN HERE 2 + 1 CELLS 1- AND WHILE 0 C, REPEAT ;

: DO8 ( --- a-addr )
\ (DO) has no inline operand, so this matches the cell version.
  POSTPONE (DO) 'LEAVE @ HERE 0 'LEAVE ! ; IMMEDIATE

: LOOP8 ( a-addr --- )
  OPERAND-ALIGN POSTPONE (LOOP) HERE - , RESOLVE-LEAVE 'LEAVE ! ; IMMEDIATE

: +LOOP8 ( a-addr --- )
  OPERAND-ALIGN POSTPONE (+LOOP) HERE - , RESOLVE-LEAVE 'LEAVE ! ; IMMEDIATE

\ ---- ?DO and LEAVE ---------------------------------------------------
\ (?DO) and (LEAVE) also carry an inline CELL operand, so they need the
\ same alignment as (LOOP).
: ?DO8 ( --- a-addr )
  OPERAND-ALIGN POSTPONE (?DO) 'LEAVE @ HERE 'LEAVE ! 0 , HERE ; IMMEDIATE

: LEAVE8 ( --- )
  OPERAND-ALIGN POSTPONE (LEAVE) HERE 'LEAVE @ , 'LEAVE ! ; IMMEDIATE

\ ---- DOES> -----------------------------------------------------------
\ A DOES> word's body is [DODOES][2-byte call to the tail][pad][PFA],
\ where the cell version wrote a single relative-call cell. CREATE8 has
\ already laid down [DOVAR][pad], so there is room to overwrite.

: !CALL ( a-addr target --- )
\ Store a call to target at a-addr, in the form CV8-DOES-FAR? selects.
\
\ The two-byte near form has a 14-bit field of SCALED units: 131 KB of
\ reach at a scale of 3, but only 16 KB at a scale of 0. Cross-compiling
\ the kernel grows the dictionary well past 16 KB, so at scale 0 a DOES>
\ word up there had its target silently truncated and jumped into the
\ data stack. The far form is three bytes, which is why CREATE has to
\ reserve a matching amount - see CV8-DOES-RESERVE.
  \ tag 2: always the 4-byte form, 11 + 30 bits, high byte first, in the 4
  \ bytes CREATE reserved (the engine's DODOES reads exactly that)
  START @ -                         ( a-addr v )
  2DUP 255 AND SWAP 3 + C!
  2DUP 8 RSHIFT 255 AND SWAP 2 + C!
  2DUP 16 RSHIFT 255 AND SWAP 1+ C!
  24 RSHIFT 192 OR SWAP C! ;

: (;CODE)8 ( --- )
\ Runtime for DOES>: point the last created word at the code following
\ the call to this word, and end the defining word (the R> discards its
\ return address, exactly as the cell version does).
  \ ALIGNED because DOES>8 pads to the next call-target boundary: the
  \ return address points at the pad, the tail starts after it.
  R> ALIGNED LAST @ NAME>
  DODOES-OP OVER C!
  1+ SWAP !CALL ;

: DOES>8 ( --- )
  \ The tail must be an ALIGNED call target: a call is a SCALED offset,
  \ so an unaligned tail address loses its low bits and jumps to the
  \ wrong place. The pad is dead code - (;CODE) never returns here.
  POSTPONE (;CODE) ALIGN POSTPONE R> ; IMMEDIATE

\ ---- debugging aid --------------------------------------------------
: BYTES. ( a-addr n --- )
\ Print n bytes from a-addr. Compiled by the CELL compiler and
\ translated, so it works even when the runtime compiler is broken.
  0 DO DUP I + C@ . LOOP DROP CR ;
